WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.160
Police! Get down!
Nobody move! Let me see your hands!

2
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.880
Hands on your head!

3
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.800
Get down. get down!

4
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.760
Automatic weapon!

5
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.920
-Go. go!
-Hands on your head!

6
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.880
-Target down.
-Stay down!

7
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.680
Target neutralized.

8
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.320
Police!

9
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.720
Police. open up!

10
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.920
Police. open up!

11
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.640
Explosive set. Ready.

12
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.800
Three.

13
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.200
Two.

14
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.200
One.

15
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.920
Nice work. man.

16
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.720
"Valère in position!"
I get the go. and boom!

17
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.040
They said there's someone
waiting for you at the gate.

18
00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.360
Okay. Uh. Cédric. could you give me
something real to do in the next…

19
00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.360
Listen. um. Max.

20
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.200
You're a good teammate. and I mean it.
I'm not bullshitting.

21
00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.456
In a couple of weeks
they'll decide what's next for you.

22
00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.360
I don't know what that is.
but we both know you're finished here.

23
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.640
My job is to make sure the section works
without you and David. okay?

24
00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.560
So why would I want to include you. huh?

25
00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.280
But take a break. Go see your visitor.

26
00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.560
ELITE FORCE

27
00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.280
Hey. this is Manon's voice mail.
If I didn't pick up…

28
00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.600
I told her to leave her phone on.
She didn't leave it on.

29
00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.400
I don't know if she's going
straight to school or if she's at Nina's.

30
00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.240
Are they taking the bus?
Do they need a drive?

31
00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.640
Let me look after Manon.
Stop worrying and go to work.

32
00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.880
It'll give me the chance
to follow my dream

33
00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.440
of becoming the world's
most accomplished stay-at-home father.

34
00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.440
Keep in mind. I can work on it
here in Paris. or in Hong Kong. same diff.

35
00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:56.520
Singapore.

36
00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.400
Hong Kong. Singapore. you decide.

37
00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:01.360
So. you got this?

38
00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.440
Absolutely. piece of cake.

39
00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.640
-Take your phone.
-Oh. right.

40
00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:11.720
-Your coffee?
-Thanks.

41
00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.440
Thanks. you're sweet.

42
00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.320
I love you.

43
00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.760
Your father had just joined the force
with David.

44
00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.560
David hadn't met Jess yet.

45
00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.440
We weren't even your age.
We were still kids.

46
00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.360
Laurent was deployed
for four months in New Caledonia.

47
00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.680
And because of my job. I couldn't go.

48
00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.880
A while after he came back.
I noticed I was late.

49
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.080
I did a test. I was pregnant. with you.

50
00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.080
We were overjoyed.

51
00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.600
Our parents thought we were too young
but we didn't care.

52
00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:53.080
The day you were born
was the happiest day of our lives.

53
00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.680
You were growing up

54
00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.600
and we wanted to give you
a little brother. or a little sister.

55
00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:05.200
We tried again.
For weeks and months. It didn't work.

56
00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.480
We went to see a specialist.
and we learned the truth.

57
00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.440
Laurent was unable to have children.

58
00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.240
Up to then. I'd always thought
Laurent was your father.

59
00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.160
Why are you telling me all this?

60
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.960
So I'll forgive you? Is that it?

61
00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.920
So I say. "It's no big deal. Mom"?

62
00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.600
I don't need your forgiveness.

63
00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.736
Having you was the best thing
that ever happened to me.

64
00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.640
-I won't apologize for that.
-But you lied to me. you…

65
00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:41.160
You cheated on Dad.

66
00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.280
With David?

67
00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.400
Why didn't you tell me
the truth after he died?

68
00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.000
Would it have helped you to know?

69
00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.760
I just wanted to protect you. I…

70
00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:53.160
Of course it would have helped me.
I have a father who's alive!

71
00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.840
I had the right to know!

72
00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.240
I was the one
who kept David out of your life.

73
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.200
What?

74
00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.880
Your father died
because David told him everything.

75
00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.800
What right did he have
to see you after that?

76
00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.120
Because of that one time. 25 years ago?

77
00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.640
You stole my father from me.
don't you understand?

78
00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.280
You had no fucking right!

79
00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:27.960
Ah. fuck.

80
00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.200
Max!

81
00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.800
Oh. shit…

82
00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.560
Yeah?

83
00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.480
David. it's Valère.
Where's your daughter right now?

84
00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.440
What is this?
Why are you asking about my daughter?

85
00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.640
Her music school.

86
00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.760
There's a hostage situation.
but we don't know who's inside.

87
00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:14.120
FRENCH ARMY

88
00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.320
Airborne on approach.
Target confirmed.

89
00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.600
Sir. sir. you can't go through.

90
00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.040
Okay. it's fine.

91
00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.160
Fox 1 in position.

92
00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.040
Fox 3 in position.

93
00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.800
This is Delta 5.
we're at security.

94
00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.720
Entrances have been rigged
with explosives.

95
00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.680
Identification in progress.

96
00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.040
Copy that.

97
00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:25.120
We're maintaining position
above the target.

98
00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.680
Check if the command post
has a list of hostages. okay?

99
00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.560
-Okay.
-A quick briefing. everyone.

100
00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.720
The van parked out front.
it's been there overnight.

101
00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.200
-I'll check it out.
-Sure. go ahead.

102
00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:40.760
So. listen up.

103
00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.760
They arrived yesterday
and spent the night there.

104
00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.400
They have assault weapons.
They're masked and prepared.

105
00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.040
At 9:00 a.m. they started shooting.

106
00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.600
Two people were wounded.
but they managed to escape.

107
00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.160
Since then.
we've heard nothing from the terrorists.

108
00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.400
We assume they're holed up
inside somewhere.

109
00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.000
We've set up these three fire supports.
All on the roof of the station. okay?

110
00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.680
Have we identified the Oscars?

111
00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:02.880
-We're expecting that any minute now.
-And where are we on tactical assault?

112
00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.040
Nowhere yet. I have no visibility.

113
00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.240
We have a 55 on the targets?

114
00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.240
Fuck. Are we in contact
with them. at least?

115
00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.480
They're not answering our calls.
They're well-prepared.

116
00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.240
Thanks. David. I know what I'm doing.

117
00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:16.440
Here are my concerns.

118
00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:20.000
They have hostages.
but they haven't made any demands.

119
00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.880
We don't know what they want.
but we know what we have to do.

120
00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.840
Get your teams together
and be ready to move in. Let's do it.

121
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.560
-We're in contact with building security.
-Calling them now.

122
00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:35.680
Okay. come on.
I need that hostage list.

123
00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.240
Hang on. here it is.

124
00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.960
-We're good. we got the list.
-Print it out. please.

125
00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:44.320
I'm with them now.

126
00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.120
We don't know if she's inside yet.

127
00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.440
Okay. so what do you know?

128
00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:52.120
Not a lot. actually.
They still haven't told me much.

129
00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.600
But of course. as soon as I get something.
I'll let you know.

130
00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:58.000
Okay. Maybe I should try Nina again.
I can't reach her either.

131
00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:05.360
-Hold on.
-What is it?

132
00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:17.400
She's in there.

133
00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:18.720
Huh?

134
00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:32.720
She's my baby.

135
00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.240
Jess.

136
00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:39.600
Jess. I'm gonna get her out.

137
00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.680
I promise. You hear me?

138
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.120
I promise you.

139
00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.080
Call you back.

140
00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.600
No. no. no. no. wait. wait!

141
00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:56.440
David!

142
00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.160
David!

143
00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.960
What are you doing?
Thinking of going in alone?

144
00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:04.760
Leave this to us.
We know what we're doing.

145
00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:05.960
Oh. yeah?

146
00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.040
Why haven't you formed
a tactical column already?

147
00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.200
We don't know
how many terrorists there are.

148
00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:12.680
They've rigged doors.
We don't know where to send in a column.

149
00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:15.320
I didn't say send in a column.
I said you should form one!

150
00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:18.136
If you send in a column at the last second
and you haven't formed one.

151
00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:19.000
you lost 30 seconds.

152
00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:20.440
We don't even know where they are!

153
00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.320
We have no videos.
nobody's talked to them.

154
00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:24.560
We have no clue what they want.
We're not ready.

155
00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.640
Hey! I'm not an idiot. Manon's in there.
but you're not running things.

156
00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.800
That's my job. okay?
You have to let me do it.

157
00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:34.600
Oh. that's fine. You've made it
very clear that you're in command.

158
00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:35.520
Here's what we'll do.

159
00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.600
You worry about your team.
I'll worry about myself.

160
00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:41.000
Cool it. Calm down. There's no fucking way
I'm letting you in there and you know it.

161
00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.520
Get the fuck off me!

162
00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:56.800
I'm sorry.

163
00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.200
I'm sorry. Cédric.

164
00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:03.160
You're emotional.

165
00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:06.360
It's normal. but it's messing you up.

166
00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:08.840
You're gonna have to trust me. okay?
Look at me.

167
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.400
We'll get every last hostage out of there.
safe and sound.

168
00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:14.760
Okay?

169
00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.520
-Yeah.
-If you're working with us. focus.

170
00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:20.960
You're the one who knows the layout.
Can you focus? Can you keep it together?

171
00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:22.120
I'm good.

172
00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.520
I'm good.

173
00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:24.680
So. let's go.

174
00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.480
Get back to work. Show time's over. guys.

175
00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:32.840
Witnesses report that several men.
all masked and heavily armed.

176
00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.520
burst into the conservatory
at around 9:00 this morning

177
00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:36.920
and took students hostage.

178
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.120
Police are already on the scene.

179
00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:42.200
We have no further information yet
about what is clearly a major operation.

180
00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:44.520
We're waiting to hear
whether authorities set up

181
00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:46.880
a direct line of communication
with the hostage takers

182
00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.360
in order to begin negotiations.

183
00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:50.440
So far the hostage takers
remain a mystery.

184
00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.800
We don't know the group's name
or what they are demanding.

185
00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:58.120
We have a chopper
hovering in this location.

186
00:11:58.200 --> 00:11:59.360
but it can't stay there long.

187
00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:01.920
We have to move fast.
I also sent out a drone.

188
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.640
We know that every entrance
is rigged with explosives.

189
00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:07.280
With all these windows.
they can see us coming. Except here.

190
00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:09.640
There's a blind spot in this building.

191
00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:12.560
You see all the green here?
Those are telecommunications cables.

192
00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:16.320
If we plug into them. we'll be able
to use all the security cameras.

193
00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:18.880
-Is that the rest of the network?
-Yeah.

194
00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.336
This is where we plug in.
which means we put the column here.

195
00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:23.120
Valère. take whoever you need
from section 1.

196
00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.560
Set up a tactical column there.

197
00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:27.640
Okay. Can I have one of your guys
to hook me up to the cameras?

198
00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.760
Yeah. sure. Uh. Rapha?

199
00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:31.520
-Can you go with Valère?
-No problem.

200
00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:34.200
-Take whatever gear you need.
-Okay.

201
00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:35.960
I'll go back to tracking the van.

202
00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.120
Cédric gave me the okay
to take part in the mission.

203
00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:54.760
I'm really sorry about Manon.

204
00:12:58.280 --> 00:12:59.680
She's my little sister.

205
00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:02.280
We'll get her out of there. Don't worry.

206
00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:03.520
Stay strong.

207
00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:13.640
Yeah? Yeah. I'm coming. I'm on my way.

208
00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.200
I'm not leaving. officer.

209
00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.320
I've told you three times now.
You have to back up.

210
00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.400
She's with me.

211
00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:24.680
She's with me!

212
00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:25.760
Okay.

213
00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:28.360
Open up. Let her through. guys.

214
00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:44.480
Right. focus up.

215
00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.480
Lock in. guys.

216
00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.240
Move out.

217
00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:11.320
My girl's here. so I'm here.

218
00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.800
Jess. will you stay in the car?

219
00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:18.080
Okay.

220
00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.160
I'll be back.

221
00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:21.760
With Manon.

222
00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:23.920
I know.

223
00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:39.000
-Do you see the hostages?
-Negative. I do not.

224
00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:50.136
Family members
are just starting to arrive on the scene.

225
00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:53.600
where a crisis team has been set up
to provide psychological support.

226
00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:55.520
Clearly. the families are feeling shock…

227
00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:00.360
We just entered at door 3.

228
00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:01.760
50 yards to the lobby.

229
00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.520
How's it going. Cédric?

230
00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:17.280
Should have access soon.
Pull up the images.

231
00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:18.480
Valère?

232
00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.440
-What's your status?
-Entering the lobby.

233
00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:33.680
Backup in position.

234
00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:02.440
We're in position.

235
00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:05.280
-Okay.
-We're good.

236
00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:17.000
Connecting.

237
00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:34.280
-Link established.
-We're in.

238
00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:37.560
Oscars and Tangos in the auditorium.
Three armed Tangos. Nine Oscars in hoods.

239
00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.240
-Hostages bunched together.
-Check the other camera feeds.

240
00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:43.840
We're taking fire!

241
00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:45.760
Rapha!

242
00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:48.360
Two officers down.
I repeat. we have two officers down!

243
00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.040
Valère. take cover! Everyone out of there!
Pull back. pull back!

244
00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:52.560
Shots fired!

245
00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:53.960
We got you. Rapha. okay?

246
00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:06.600
We have shots fired!

247
00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:09.040
You okay?
Are you okay? Can you hear me?

248
00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.400
It's gotta be
from the building next door. Cédric!

249
00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:14.400
We're evacuating.
we're evacuating.

250
00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:15.480
Go on.

251
00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:17.640
Schwepps. two pairs with me!

252
00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:20.600
